#====================================================================
# E261 — Rollback must retain the old output on an untrusted target
#====================================================================

id:                     E261
trigger_tool:           native-image|runtime|test_package
phase:                  runtime|rollback|testing
error_signature:        installed Native Image output must not be a symlink|Native Image output changed during install|Native Image transaction rollback failed|signed-output.*without.*recovery

severity:               3
category:               native-image|finalizer|rollback|security|transaction
match_keywords:         native-image, finalizer, rollback, recovery, symlink, identity, signed-output, renameat2, RENAME_NOREPLACE, concurrent replacement
title:                  Transaction rollback must retain the old output when the installed target is untrusted

root_cause:             After an exchange commit the backup path carries the previous user output. If rollback trusts only the path, catches only OSError, or cleans temporaries unconditionally, a concurrent symlink, non-regular object, identity error, or same-byte replacement can bypass recovery and cause the previous output to be deleted.
affected_scope:         Signed finalizers and transactional packagers that exchange a staged artifact into a public target while retaining the previous target in a temporary backup until commit durability is proven.
verification_cmd:       Replace the installed target after exchange with regular, symlink, and injected identity-error objects; require the concurrent target to remain untouched, exactly one verified old-output recovery file, and no path-only cleanup deletion.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           identity-bound-recovery-and-cleanup
rec_description:        Verify both exchange sides, treat OS and domain identity errors as recovery conditions, move the old-output backup to a unique no-replace recovery path, revalidate it, and clean only identities recorded by the current invocation.
rec_command:            Add identity-bound recovery around installed-target checks and reopen the committed target with no-follow semantics after directory fsync.
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               source-patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      fail-closed-leave-backup
fallback_description:   When recovery identity cannot be proven, fail without deleting the backup path; a recoverable leftover is safer than losing the previous output.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          source-patch

forbid_1_pattern:       except OSError.*identity|for temporary in temporaries:.*unlink
forbid_1_reason:        Identity checks can raise domain errors, and path-only cleanup is not bound to the object created by the current transaction.
forbid_1_consequence:   Rollback can delete the previous user output or a concurrently replaced object.

principles:             P017

causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             E260
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               doc/E261.md
last_updated:           2026-08-08
source_event:           GraalVM 25.0.3 PR #3928 Native Image rollback and post-fsync identity closure

authors:                2301_80739235 <2047361658@qq.com>
